NOTE=Follow-up applied: unique_dir()'s collision (flagged 03:05) fixed with the same monotonic AtomicU64 pattern as worktree::unique_name; 20/20 default-parallelism runs green, --test-threads=1 unaffected. || Second follow-up (11:35): closed a real retry dead-end in RealChangeEmitter::emit -- a gh hiccup (exit 0, no URL, PR_URL_ABSENT) after the branch push already succeeded left the task Accepted but permanently unretryable, because a retry re-applies the identical attested diff onto the identical base, producing a sibling commit that a plain push rejects as non-fast-forward on the deterministic fleet/<task> branch. Fixed with --force on that push (justification: wt.branch is the agent's own disposable proposal branch, never shared -- this code path only runs while the task is still Accepted, i.e. before any PR exists on that branch, so nothing else has a legitimate reason to have pushed to it). New regression test tests/f08_pr_emit.rs::retry_after_gh_partial_failure_succeeds_without_manual_branch_deletion, driven with a stateful gh shim (fails call 1, succeeds call 2); confirmed RED pre-fix (fails with the exact real-world code PR_EMIT_FAILED) and GREEN post-fix by toggling the fix locally. cargo test -p fleet --lib: 12/12. cargo test -p fleet --test f08_pr_emit -- --test-threads=1: 5/5 (incl. the 4 pre-existing tests, unmodified assertions). lifecycle.rs untouched (scoped to RealChangeEmitter per task). This increment is self-tested only (same session built and ran its own tests) -- not yet independently re-derived by a separate verifier pass, per this repo's own builder!=verifier convention; flagging for that pass. See FLEET-LEARNINGS.md.
